<h4 style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;color:#1=
2395b;margin:16px 0 6px;">Acadia=E2=80=99s Alzheimer=E2=80=99s-psychosis prog=
ram now requires Phase 3 rescue rather than confirmation</h4>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What changed</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Remlifanserin 60 mg reduced the SAPS h=
allucinations-and-delusions score by 12.6 points versus 10.4 with placebo at =
week six, missing the primary endpoint with an effect size of 0.26 and <em>p<=
/em>=3D0.0603. The clinician-rated CGI-S-ADP secondary endpoint was nominally=
 significant at <em>p</em>=3D0.0077, and Acadia reported favorable tolerabili=
ty. The company plans to continue the ongoing Phase 3 program. (<a href=3D"ht=
tps://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1070494/000119312526401157/d168737dex99=
1.htm" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">sec.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What it tells us</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The modest primary-endpoint separation=
 cannot reasonably be characterized as clinical validation. The secondary res=
ult and apparent dose effect justify further study, but they may reflect an e=
ndpoint that is more responsive=E2=80=94or more subjective=E2=80=94rather tha=
n a robust antipsychotic effect.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Acadia must now optimize Phase 3 aroun=
d placebo response, patient selection and endpoint sensitivity without appear=
ing to redesign the program around a favorable secondary analysis. Given the =
company=E2=80=99s earlier regulatory setbacks in Alzheimer=E2=80=99s psychosi=
s, FDA alignment will be especially important.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What to watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Full CTAD data in November, including =
the 30-mg arm, regional and baseline-severity subgroups, discontinuations and=
 concordance across symptom measures; any Phase 3 protocol changes; and wheth=
er FDA accepts CGI-based evidence as supportive rather than primary.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;color:#1=
2395b;margin:16px 0 6px;">Autoimmune development is rewarding phenotype-speci=
fic mechanisms</h4>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Amgen=E2=80=99s approximately 621-pati=
ent OASIZ 301 trial met its week-48 ESSDAI primary endpoint for dazodalibep i=
n moderate-to-severe systemic Sj=C3=B6gren=E2=80=99s disease, with improvemen=
t reported from week four. The result could support the first disease-modifyi=
ng option for a population defined by systemic organ activity, but Amgen has =
not disclosed effect magnitude, responder rates or detailed safety. A separat=
e Phase 3 study in patients with high symptom burden but low systemic activit=
y is due to complete in the fourth quarter. (<a href=3D"https://investors.amg=
en.com/news-releases/news-release-details/amgen-announces-positive-topline-ph=
ase-3-results-dazodalibep" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"=
>investors.amgen.com</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">In contrast, Immunovant=E2=80=99s IMVT=
-1402 failed to significantly improve CLASI-A at week 12 in cutaneous lupus, =
prompting discontinuation in that indication. The result weakens the assumpti=
on that deep IgG reduction through FcRn blockade will translate broadly acros=
s autoantibody-associated diseases. (<a href=3D"https://www.immunovant.com/in=
vestors/news-events/press-releases?utm_source=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9=
a;text-decoration:underline;">immunovant.com</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The emerging lesson is not that CD40L =
is superior to FcRn across autoimmunity. It is that mechanism, disease compar=
tment and endpoint must align: interrupting T-cell/B-cell co-stimulation may =
be particularly relevant to systemic Sj=C3=B6gren=E2=80=99s, while skin-domin=
ant lupus may not respond sufficiently to IgG lowering alone.</p>
