<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;">Bottom Line</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">This week shifted competitive attentio=
n from whether technologies work to how regulators, clinicians and patients w=
ill use them. Galleri may reach the market despite unresolved clinical utilit=
y; obesity developers are designing induction and maintenance ecosystems rath=
er than simply chasing the largest weight-loss number; and weekly insulin is =
becoming a convenience class.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The counterexamples were equally instr=
uctive. Acadia=E2=80=99s primary miss shows that a favorable secondary endpoi=
nt cannot substitute for robust efficacy, while the divergence between Sj=C3=
=B6gren=E2=80=99s and cutaneous-lupus programs reinforces that broad immunolo=
gical rationales still require disease-specific clinical validation.</p><p st=
